  "summary_en": "Japan's MIC/METI non-binding soft-law Guidelines for AI Business Operators (v1.1, March 2025), integrating three earlier guidelines. They set a risk-based, goal-based framework with common principles and role-specific duties for AI developers, providers and users, plus AI governance and advanced-AI-system guidance. Cyber-physical Society 5.0 is mentioned, but no robot-specific provisions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Non-binding, goal-based soft law to promote voluntary action and balance innovation with risk mitigation",
   "Defines three actors: AI developers, providers and business users, with role-specific duties",
   "Common guidelines: human-centricity, safety, fairness, privacy, security, transparency, accountability",
   "Adopts a risk-based approach and a living-document, agile governance update model",
   "Additional common guidance for actors handling advanced AI systems, aligned with the Hiroshima AI Process"
